/F2 10 Tf
(SECURITY WARNING) Tj
T*
(JWT creation exists, but bearer-token verification is not implemented. Spring Security currently) Tj
T*
(permits requests. User-scoped endpoints trust caller-supplied X-User-Id, which can be spoofed.) Tj
T*
(Do not expose the API to untrusted networks. Implement JWT signature/expiry/issuer validation,) Tj
T*
(derive identity from authenticated principal, remove identity headers, configure CORS, and test access.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 10 Tf
(IDEMPOTENCY LIMITATIONS) Tj
T*
(The payment key is saved as a unique transaction reference and duplicate lookup returns an existing) Tj
T*
(record. This is not fully concurrency-safe, does not verify same-key payload consistency, and has no) Tj
T*
(dedicated durable idempotency ledger. Do not process real money. A robust design needs a scoped unique) Tj
T*
(key, request fingerprint, persisted outcome, atomic payment/balance effects, locking or optimistic) Tj
T*
(concurrency, and integration tests for simultaneous retries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 10 Tf
(FRONTEND INTEGRATION) Tj
T*
(The client still has legacy API paths and a legacy base URL. Align routes, DTOs, token handling,) Tj
T*
(response/error contracts, and CORS before expecting end-to-end operation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
